---

<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="60–70 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Vocabulary · Lesson 17</p>
  <h1>Crime & society: <em>report the act, evidence, and stage without deciding guilt</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Accurate crime language answers separate questions: <span class="ex">What was reported?</span> <span class="ex">Who was affected?</span> <span class="ex">What does the evidence actually show?</span> <span class="ex">What stage has the legal process reached?</span> <span class="ex">What response could reduce harm or support the community?</span> A report can describe a serious incident without turning an allegation into a fact or a suspect into a convicted person.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">60–70 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">theft · robbery · burglary · fraud</span>
    <span class="tag">evidence · allegation · legal process</span>
    <span class="tag">15–20 min listening and retrieval</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Separate a reported incident, observable evidence, an investigation, and a public claim.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Distinguish</b><span>Track what was taken or damaged, who was affected, and which legal stage has been reached.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Calibrate</b><span>Use alleged, according to, appears to, charged with, and convicted of at the right level of certainty.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Respond</b><span>Give a neutral briefing and propose a measurable, fair community response.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can distinguish theft, robbery, burglary, vandalism, fraud, identity theft, and related offenses; use steal, rob, break into, accuse, charge, convict, and sentence with their natural patterns; keep victim, witness, suspect, defendant, and convicted offender distinct; describe evidence without claiming more than it supports; interpret reported-crime data cautiously; make key U.S. pronunciations and stress contrasts audible; and deliver a neutral fictional community-safety briefing with a fair, measurable response.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You recovered a past passive, a cautious deduction from incomplete evidence, and a source-evidence distinction from the prerequisite lessons.">
    <h3>Reactivate passive focus, deduction, and source checking</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Crime reporting foundation choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Two bicycles were stolen outside the station last night">Two bicycles were stolen outside the station last night</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="might be the scheduled repair technician">might be the scheduled repair technician</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the police report is the source and the timestamped video is evidence">the police report is the source and the timestamped video is evidence</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="must be guilty because the window is broken">must be guilty because the window is broken</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Make the affected property the focus: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Two bicycles were stolen outside the station last night" data-hint="Use a past passive because the bicycles, not an unknown actor, are the useful starting point." data-fix="Two bicycles were stolen outside the station last night.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>A person beside the broken window has a repair-company uniform, tools, and an appointment in the building log. Before checking the appointment, the person <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="might be the scheduled repair technician" data-hint="The clues support a possibility, but the appointment has not been confirmed yet." data-fix="The person might be the scheduled repair technician.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>In a report that quotes a police document and links to timestamped video, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the police report is the source and the timestamped video is evidence" data-hint="A source supplies information; evidence supports or tests a claim." data-fix="The police report is the source, and the timestamped video is evidence for the claim.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice five different claims in one incident update</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Fictional Northside Community Hub update</h3>
    <p><b>Facility record:</b> <span class="ex">“At 6:45 Monday morning, an employee found the rear storage-door frame damaged and three loaner laptops missing.”</span></p>
    <p><b>Security record:</b> <span class="ex">“Video shows a person entering the storage hallway at 2:18 a.m., but the camera does not show the person’s face or the laptops being removed.”</span></p>
    <p><b>Police update:</b> <span class="ex">“Police are investigating a suspected burglary. No one has been arrested or charged.”</span></p>
    <p><b>Uncorrected neighborhood post:</b> <span class="ex">“The laptop thief has been caught.”</span></p>
    <p><b>Hub response:</b> <span class="ex">“The damaged frame was repaired, and the hub added an inventory check and brighter rear lighting.”</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which statements are direct records, and which statement makes an unsupported claim?</li>
      <li>What does the video show, and what does it not show?</li>
      <li>Has the legal process reached arrest, charge, trial, or conviction?</li>
      <li>Which actions respond to security without claiming that they will prevent every future incident?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You separated the observed damage and missing property, limited video evidence, open investigation, and unsupported caught claim.">
    <h3>Discovery check: what does each statement establish?</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Northside incident claim choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="damaged door frame and three missing laptops">damaged door frame and three missing laptops</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a person entered the hallway at 2:18 but was not identified">a person entered the hallway at 2:18 but was not identified</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="an investigation is open and no one has been arrested or charged">an investigation is open and no one has been arrested or charged</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="an unsupported claim that someone was caught">an unsupported claim that someone was caught</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="proof that the lighting caused every later outcome">proof that the lighting caused every later outcome</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The employee’s direct observation establishes a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="damaged door frame and three missing laptops" data-hint="Use only what the employee found at 6:45." data-fix="The employee found a damaged door frame and three missing laptops.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The complete security-video statement establishes that <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a person entered the hallway at 2:18 but was not identified" data-hint="Keep both the visible action and the limit of the camera image." data-fix="A person entered the hallway at 2:18, but the video did not identify the person.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The police update establishes that <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an investigation is open and no one has been arrested or charged" data-hint="Do not advance beyond the two legal stages explicitly denied in the update." data-fix="An investigation is open, and no one has been arrested or charged.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The neighborhood post contains <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an unsupported claim that someone was caught" data-hint="Compare caught with the police statement that no one has been arrested." data-fix="The post makes an unsupported claim that someone was caught.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Name the reported act without collapsing nearby meanings</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p><span class="ex">Crime</span> can name the general social problem, as in <span class="ex">reported crime fell</span>, or one countable act, as in <span class="ex">a crime was reported</span>. An <span class="ex">offense</span> is an act prohibited by law. The everyday distinctions below are useful for reporting, but exact legal definitions and categories vary by jurisdiction.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>term</th><th>central idea in this lesson</th><th>natural frame</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">theft</span></td><td>taking property without permission; force or unlawful entry is not part of the basic word</td><td><span class="ex">report a theft · phone theft · theft from a vehicle</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">robbery</span></td><td>taking property from a person or place through force or threat</td><td><span class="ex">an armed robbery · report a robbery at a store</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">burglary</span></td><td>unlawful entry into a building or other covered place with intent to commit an offense</td><td><span class="ex">investigate a burglary · a suspected burglary</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">shoplifting</span></td><td>taking goods from a store without paying</td><td><span class="ex">report suspected shoplifting</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">vandalism</span></td><td>intentional damage to property</td><td><span class="ex">repair damage caused by vandalism</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">fraud</span></td><td>deception used to obtain money, property, or another benefit</td><td><span class="ex">suspected payment fraud · commit fraud</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">identity theft</span></td><td>using another person’s identifying information without permission, often for fraud</td><td><span class="ex">report identity theft · protect personal information</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">cybercrime</span></td><td>a broad category for offenses involving computers, accounts, or networks</td><td><span class="ex">investigate cybercrime · a cybercrime unit</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line"><b>Boundary:</b> Everyday news labels can be less exact than legal charges. When the official category is not known, describe the observed act or say <span class="ex">reported theft</span>, <span class="ex">suspected fraud</span>, or <span class="ex">police are investigating</span> instead of inventing a charge.</p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You classified taking without force, force or threat, unlawful entry, property damage, and deceptive payment by their supplied facts.">
    <h3>Classify the act from the complete context</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Offense classification choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="theft">theft</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="robbery">robbery</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="burglary">burglary</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="vandalism">vandalism</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="fraud">fraud</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="shoplifting">shoplifting</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>A phone disappeared from an unlocked desk while its owner was at lunch. No force, threat, or unlawful entry is reported. The basic act described is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="theft" data-hint="Property was taken without permission, and the context supplies no force or entry element." data-fix="The basic act described is theft.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>A person threatened a cashier and demanded money from the register. The act described is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="robbery" data-hint="The decisive cue is the threat used to take money." data-fix="The threat used to take money makes this a robbery in the lesson’s everyday distinction.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Someone forced open a closed office window and entered intending to steal computers. The act described is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="burglary" data-hint="The context supplies unlawful entry into a building and criminal intent." data-fix="The act described is burglary under the lesson’s general distinction, subject to local legal definitions.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Someone deliberately painted over the community center’s signs but took nothing. The act described is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="vandalism" data-hint="The context centers on intentional property damage rather than taking property." data-fix="The act described is vandalism.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>A fake invoice persuaded a business to send payment to an account controlled by the sender. The deception for financial benefit is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="fraud" data-hint="The payment was obtained through a deliberately false invoice." data-fix="The described deception for payment is fraud.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Track the thing, place, and affected person through the verb pattern</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>pattern</th><th>focus</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">steal + thing</span></td><td>the property taken</td><td><span class="ex">Someone stole a laptop from the office.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">steal + thing + from + person/place</span></td><td>property first, then its source</td><td><span class="ex">A phone was stolen from a passenger.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">rob + person/place</span></td><td>the person or institution targeted through force or threat</td><td><span class="ex">Someone robbed the store. The cashier was robbed.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">break into + building/vehicle/account</span></td><td>unauthorized entry in everyday language</td><td><span class="ex">Someone broke into the office.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">commit + crime/offense/fraud</span></td><td>performing the prohibited act</td><td><span class="ex">The report does not establish who committed the offense.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p><span class="ex">My apartment was robbed</span> is common in informal speech, but precise editing usually makes the relationship clearer: <span class="ex">Someone broke into my apartment</span> or <span class="ex">My apartment was burglarized</span>. A thing is <span class="ex">stolen</span>; a person or place is <span class="ex">robbed</span>. <span class="ex">Burglarize</span> is standard U.S. English, while <span class="ex">break into</span> is often more natural in conversation.</p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You kept stolen property, robbed people or institutions, unauthorized entry, offense collocation, and uncountable evidence in their natural frames.">
    <h3>Choose the frame that preserves each participant</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Crime verb pattern choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="stole two tablets from the hub">stole two tablets from the hub</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="robbed the credit union">robbed the credit union</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="broke into the locked storage room">broke into the locked storage room</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="committed the offense">committed the offense</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="three pieces of evidence">three pieces of evidence</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="stole the credit union of cash">stole the credit union of cash</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The inventory confirms which property is missing. The report says someone <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="stole two tablets from the hub" data-hint="Use steal plus the things taken, followed by from plus the source." data-fix="Someone stole two tablets from the hub.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>A person threatened the teller and demanded money from the institution. The report says the person <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="robbed the credit union" data-hint="Rob takes the affected person or institution as its object." data-fix="The person robbed the credit union.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The door had been locked, and an unknown person entered without permission. Someone <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="broke into the locked storage room" data-hint="Break into names unauthorized entry to the room." data-fix="Someone broke into the locked storage room.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The court record establishes that the defendant <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="committed the offense" data-hint="Commit naturally combines with crime, offense, and fraud." data-fix="The court record establishes that the defendant committed the offense.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The case file contains a timestamped video, an inventory record, and a damaged lock: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="three pieces of evidence" data-hint="Evidence is uncountable, so count pieces rather than evidences." data-fix="The file contains three pieces of evidence.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Keep each person inside the correct legal stage</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>A <span class="ex">victim</span> is a person harmed by an offense. A <span class="ex">witness</span> has relevant information or observed something. A <span class="ex">suspect</span> is a person investigators believe may be connected to an offense. A <span class="ex">defendant</span> is the person responding to a case in court. <span class="ex">Offender</span> can identify a person who committed an offense, so do not use it as a replacement for suspect before responsibility is established.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>stage</th><th>useful language</th><th>what it does not prove by itself</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>investigation</td><td><span class="ex">Police are investigating. A witness was interviewed.</span></td><td>who committed the act</td></tr>
      <tr><td>arrest</td><td><span class="ex">A suspect was arrested.</span></td><td>guilt or a later charge</td></tr>
      <tr><td>charge</td><td><span class="ex">The person was charged with burglary.</span></td><td>conviction</td></tr>
      <tr><td>trial or hearing</td><td><span class="ex">The defendant appeared in court.</span></td><td>the final outcome</td></tr>
      <tr><td>verdict</td><td><span class="ex">The defendant was convicted of fraud / found not guilty / acquitted.</span></td><td>a universal explanation of everything that happened</td></tr>
      <tr><td>sentence</td><td><span class="ex">The judge sentenced the convicted defendant to community service.</span></td><td>that every jurisdiction uses the same penalty</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line"><b>Important limit:</b> Procedures, legal labels, burdens of proof, and the meaning of particular outcomes vary across legal systems. An arrest does not establish guilt, and a charge does not establish conviction. <span class="ex">Acquitted</span> or <span class="ex">found not guilty</span> means the prosecution did not obtain a conviction; it is not the same language as a separate finding that proves every possible account. This lesson teaches neutral English, not legal advice.</p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You placed the witness, suspect, defendant, conviction, and sentence at the stage stated in each complete case update.">
    <h3>Choose the role or process that the record supports</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Legal role and stage choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="witness">witness</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="suspect">suspect</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="defendant">defendant</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="convicted of fraud">convicted of fraud</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="sentenced to 100 hours of community service">sentenced to 100 hours of community service</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="criminal before any investigation">criminal before any investigation</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Lee heard glass break and gave investigators an accurate time, but Lee is not accused of the offense. Lee is a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="witness" data-hint="This person supplies relevant observed information and is not accused." data-fix="Lee is a witness.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Investigators believe a person may be connected to the incident, but no charge has been filed. The person is a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="suspect" data-hint="Possible connection during an investigation supports suspect, not a statement of guilt." data-fix="The person is a suspect.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>A charge has been filed, and the person is responding to the case in court. In that court case, the person is the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="defendant" data-hint="Use the role for the person against whom the court case is brought." data-fix="In the court case, the person is the defendant.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>After the trial, the court returned a guilty verdict on the fraud charge. The defendant was <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="convicted of fraud" data-hint="A guilty verdict establishes the conviction; use convicted of plus the offense." data-fix="The defendant was convicted of fraud.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>At the later penalty hearing, the judge ordered 100 hours of service. The defendant was <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="sentenced to 100 hours of community service" data-hint="Use sentenced to for the penalty imposed after conviction in this record." data-fix="The defendant was sentenced to 100 hours of community service.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Match the grammar to allegation, charge, and conviction</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>relationship</th><th>pattern</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>unproven reported act</td><td><span class="ex">alleged + noun / allegedly + verb</span></td><td><span class="ex">an alleged theft · The payment was allegedly diverted.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>statement against a person</td><td><span class="ex">accuse someone of + noun/-ing</span></td><td><span class="ex">The complaint accused an employee of changing the record.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>formal charge</td><td><span class="ex">charge someone with + offense</span></td><td><span class="ex">The person was charged with fraud.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>guilty verdict</td><td><span class="ex">convict someone of + offense</span></td><td><span class="ex">The defendant was convicted of fraud.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>penalty</td><td><span class="ex">sentence someone to + penalty/time</span></td><td><span class="ex">The judge sentenced the defendant to community service.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p><span class="ex">Alleged</span> normally modifies a noun: <span class="ex">an alleged scheme</span>. <span class="ex">Allegedly</span> modifies a claim about an action: <span class="ex">The account was allegedly used without permission</span>. These words attribute uncertainty; they do not prove either guilt or innocence. Prefer a clear source when available: <span class="ex">According to the complaint...</span> or <span class="ex">Police said...</span>.</p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You used alleged for an unproven noun phrase and preserved the required of, with, of, and to patterns across the legal stages.">
    <h3>Complete the relationship, not only the vocabulary word</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Legal collocation choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="alleged identity-theft scheme">alleged identity-theft scheme</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="accused the contractor of changing the invoice">accused the contractor of changing the invoice</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="charged the contractor with fraud">charged the contractor with fraud</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="convicted the contractor of fraud">convicted the contractor of fraud</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="sentenced the contractor to community service">sentenced the contractor to community service</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="charged the contractor of fraud">charged the contractor of fraud</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The complaint describes an unproven plan involving personal information as an <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="alleged identity-theft scheme" data-hint="Use alleged before the noun phrase because the scheme has not been established at this stage." data-fix="The complaint describes an alleged identity-theft scheme.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The complaint made a claim against the contractor but did not itself file a criminal charge. It <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="accused the contractor of changing the invoice" data-hint="Accuse takes a person followed by of plus a noun or -ing form." data-fix="The complaint accused the contractor of changing the invoice.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Prosecutors then filed the formal fraud charge. They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="charged the contractor with fraud" data-hint="Charge takes the person followed by with plus the offense." data-fix="Prosecutors charged the contractor with fraud.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>After a guilty verdict, the court <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="convicted the contractor of fraud" data-hint="Convict takes the person followed by of plus the offense." data-fix="The court convicted the contractor of fraud.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>At the penalty hearing, the judge <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="sentenced the contractor to community service" data-hint="Sentence takes the person followed by to plus the penalty." data-fix="The judge sentenced the contractor to community service.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Report evidence as support, not as a verdict</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p><span class="ex">Evidence</span> is uncountable: <span class="ex">some evidence, a piece of evidence, three pieces of evidence</span>. Evidence can <span class="ex">show</span> an observable detail, <span class="ex">support</span> a claim, <span class="ex">suggest</span> a possibility, <span class="ex">contradict</span> an account, or remain <span class="ex">inconclusive</span>. Its strength depends on relevance, quality, context, and how directly it supports the exact claim.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>evidence situation</th><th>defensible language</th><th>unsupported leap</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>clear timestamp, unclear identity</td><td><span class="ex">The video shows a person entering at 2:18.</span></td><td><span class="ex">The video proves who stole the laptops.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>witness heard a noise</td><td><span class="ex">A witness reported hearing glass break.</span></td><td><span class="ex">The witness identified the offender.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>object may share a source</td><td><span class="ex">The mark may link the two incidents.</span></td><td><span class="ex">The mark must prove one person committed both.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>claim conflicts with a record</td><td><span class="ex">The access log contradicts that part of the account.</span></td><td><span class="ex">Every other part is automatically false.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>checking is incomplete</td><td><span class="ex">The claim remains unverified.</span></td><td><span class="ex">Unverified means definitely true or definitely false.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line"><b>Deduction boundary:</b> <span class="ex">Must</span> can express a strong conclusion in ordinary situations, but it should not be used to declare legal guilt from a few clues. Say what the clue supports and preserve the missing step: <span class="ex">The access record suggests that the card was used at 2:10, but it does not establish who used it.</span></p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You limited the camera, witness account, tool mark, access record, and unchecked post to the exact claims each could support.">
    <h3>Calibrate the claim to the supplied evidence</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Evidence calibration choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="shows a person entering at 2:18 but does not identify the person">shows a person entering at 2:18 but does not identify the person</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="reports hearing glass break but does not identify who caused it">reports hearing glass break but does not identify who caused it</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="may link the two damaged locks but is not conclusive by itself">may link the two damaged locks but is not conclusive by itself</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="contradicts the claimed entry time but does not decide every other fact">contradicts the claimed entry time but does not decide every other fact</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="remains unverified until an accountable source or evidence supports or rejects it">remains unverified until an accountable source or evidence supports or rejects it</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="proves the nearest person committed every offense">proves the nearest person committed every offense</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The camera records the hallway, but the person’s face and the removal of the laptops are outside the image. The video <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="shows a person entering at 2:18 but does not identify the person" data-hint="State the visible entry and preserve the identity limit." data-fix="The video shows a person entering at 2:18 but does not identify the person.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>A neighbor heard glass break but saw no person or vehicle. The witness <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="reports hearing glass break but does not identify who caused it" data-hint="The account supports the sound, not an identity." data-fix="The witness reports hearing glass break but does not identify who caused it.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Two locks have a similar unusual tool mark, but investigators have not compared the tools or other records. The mark <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="may link the two damaged locks but is not conclusive by itself" data-hint="The similarity supports a possible link, not a complete conclusion." data-fix="The mark may link the two damaged locks but is not conclusive by itself.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>A statement says the card entered at 3:00, while the automatic access record shows 2:10. The record <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="contradicts the claimed entry time but does not decide every other fact" data-hint="Limit the contradiction to the entry-time claim that the record directly tests." data-fix="The record contradicts the claimed entry time but does not decide every other fact.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>An anonymous post says an arrest occurred, but the current police update reports no arrest. The post <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="remains unverified until an accountable source or evidence supports or rejects it" data-hint="Unverified describes the current checking status; it is not a final truth judgment." data-fix="The post remains unverified until an accountable source or evidence supports or rejects it.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Discuss society through harm, reporting, response, and measurement</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p><span class="ex">Reported crime</span> means incidents recorded by the source being discussed. It is not automatically identical to every incident that occurred. A change in reported numbers may reflect a real change, willingness to report, access to reporting, recording rules, enforcement priorities, or several factors together. A responsible explanation names the source, place, offense category, timeframe, comparison, and limitation.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>response purpose</th><th>examples</th><th>evaluation question</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>support people affected</td><td>replacement documents, counseling referral, safe reporting, practical information</td><td>Did affected people reach useful support without unnecessary barriers?</td></tr>
      <tr><td>reduce opportunity</td><td>better locks, lighting, secure storage, account protection</td><td>Did the targeted incident type change at comparable places and times?</td></tr>
      <tr><td>improve fair process</td><td>accurate records, interpreters, evidence standards, accountable review</td><td>Was the process accessible, consistent, and based on relevant evidence?</td></tr>
      <tr><td>reduce repeated harm</td><td>education, treatment, supervised support, rehabilitation, community programs</td><td>What outcome changed, for whom, and over what period?</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">Prevention language should not blame a victim for another person’s conduct. <span class="ex">A stronger lock could reduce one opportunity</span> describes a practical measure; it does not transfer responsibility for the offense to the person whose property was taken. A proposal also needs a limit, cost, fairness check, and measure of success.</p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You kept reported incidents distinct from all incidents, preserved the denominator, avoided causal overclaiming, centered victim support, and chose a measurable prevention pilot.">
    <h3>Interpret the community record without manufacturing a conclusion</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Community response choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="incidents recorded by the stated reporting system">incidents recorded by the stated reporting system</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="12 reports out of 800 registered bicycles">12 reports out of 800 registered bicycles</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="may reflect the new reporting form as well as any change in incidents">may reflect the new reporting form as well as any change in incidents</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="offer practical support without assigning responsibility to the victim">offer practical support without assigning responsibility to the victim</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="pilot secure parking and compare reports, use, cost, and access for six months">pilot secure parking and compare reports, use, cost, and access for six months</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="proof that one poster ended all crime">proof that one poster ended all crime</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>In a transit-agency table, <span class="ex">reported bicycle theft</span> refers to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="incidents recorded by the stated reporting system" data-hint="Reported names the records in the supplied system, not every event that may have occurred." data-fix="Reported bicycle theft refers to incidents recorded by the stated reporting system.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The station registered 800 bicycles and recorded 12 theft reports during the quarter. The clearest rate context is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="12 reports out of 800 registered bicycles" data-hint="Keep the number of reports with the relevant population supplied in the record." data-fix="The record contains 12 reports out of 800 registered bicycles.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The agency introduced an easier online report form in the same month that recorded reports rose. The rise <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="may reflect the new reporting form as well as any change in incidents" data-hint="Two conditions changed, so do not assign the entire increase to one cause." data-fix="The rise may reflect the new reporting form as well as any change in incidents.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>After a theft report, the service desk should <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="offer practical support without assigning responsibility to the victim" data-hint="Support the affected person while keeping responsibility for the act with the person who committed it." data-fix="The service desk should offer practical support without assigning responsibility to the victim.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The station wants to test secure bicycle parking before expanding it. A defensible next step is to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="pilot secure parking and compare reports, use, cost, and access for six months" data-hint="Choose the response with a defined action, timeframe, relevant outcomes, cost, and access measure." data-fix="Pilot secure parking and compare reports, use, cost, and access for six months.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Sound natural: make the offense, role, and certainty boundary audible</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p><span class="ex">Theft</span> /θɛft/ ends with a difficult /ft/ cluster: hold the lower lip lightly against the upper teeth for /f/, then release the /t/. U.S. <span class="ex">burglary</span> is usually three syllables, /ˈbɝɡləri/, with stress on <span class="ex">BUR</span>. <span class="ex">Evidence</span> /ˈɛvədəns/ begins with stress and is not pronounced like <span class="ex">evidences</span>.</p>
  <p>The noun <span class="ex">SUSpect</span> has first-syllable stress; the verb <span class="ex">susPECT</span> has second-syllable stress. The same shift occurs in <span class="ex">a CONvict</span> and <span class="ex">to conVICT</span>. In <span class="ex">charged with</span>, the final sounds connect across the word boundary. In <span class="ex">A suspect was ARRESTED, but no one has been CONVICTED</span>, stress the legal stages that correct the listener’s assumption.</p>
  <section data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read offense sounds, noun-verb stress, legal collocations, evidence limits, reported-crime scope, and contrastive legal-stage listening check">
    <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You heard the theft cluster, noun-verb suspect stress, charged-with relationship, evidence limit, and arrested-versus-convicted contrast.">
      <h3>Tutor-read listening: recover the sound and the legal meaning</h3>
      <p class="note-line">The tutor reads each line once naturally and once with the key contrast emphasized. The learner answers before seeing the written line again.</p>
      <div class="quiz-list">
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The final /ft/ cluster belongs to theft." data-hint="Listen for /f/ immediately followed by /t/ at the end of the offense noun." data-fix="The final /ft/ cluster belongs to theft."><p class="quiz-question">1. Tutor line: “The theft was reported after lunch.” Which sound closes the offense noun?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The final /ft/ cluster belongs to theft.">The final /ft/ cluster belongs to theft.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The word ends with a separate extra syllable, thefted.">The word ends with a separate extra syllable, thefted.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The word ends with /bər/ because it means robbery.">The word ends with /bər/ because it means robbery.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The first is the noun for a person; the second is the verb for believing possible involvement." data-hint="Listen for SUS-pect first and sus-PECT second." data-fix="The first is the noun suspect; the second is the verb suspect."><p class="quiz-question">2. Tutor line: “A SUSpect was interviewed, but police do not yet susPECT that person committed the theft.” What does the stress change mark?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The first is the noun for a person; the second is the verb for believing possible involvement.">The first is the noun for a person; the second is the verb for believing possible involvement.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Both words are past-tense forms meaning convicted.">Both words are past-tense forms meaning convicted.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The stress proves the person is guilty.">The stress proves the person is guilty.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The formal accusation is fraud; the sentence does not report a conviction." data-hint="Charged with names the filed offense but stops before a guilty verdict." data-fix="The person was charged with fraud, not reported as convicted of it."><p class="quiz-question">3. Tutor line: “The person was charged with fraud on Tuesday.” What legal relationship is stated?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The formal accusation is fraud; the sentence does not report a conviction.">The formal accusation is fraud; the sentence does not report a conviction.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A judge imposed a final penalty on Tuesday.">A judge imposed a final penalty on Tuesday.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A witness admitted committing fraud.">A witness admitted committing fraud.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The access card was used at 2:10, but the record does not identify the user." data-hint="Keep the logged action and the missing identity together." data-fix="The record shows card use at 2:10 but does not identify who used it."><p class="quiz-question">4. Tutor line: “The record SHOWS the card was used at 2:10; it does NOT show who used it.” What evidence boundary is emphasized?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The access card was used at 2:10, but the record does not identify the user.">The access card was used at 2:10, but the record does not identify the user.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The record identifies and convicts the user.">The record identifies and convicts the user.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="No card was used because the user is unknown.">No card was used because the user is unknown.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Arrest occurred, but conviction has not occurred." data-hint="Listen for contrastive stress on arrested and not convicted." data-fix="The sentence reports an arrest and explicitly denies a conviction so far."><p class="quiz-question">5. Tutor line: “A suspect was ARRESTED, but has NOT been CONVICTED.” Which two stages are contrasted?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Arrest occurred, but conviction has not occurred.">Arrest occurred, but conviction has not occurred.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Conviction occurred before any investigation.">Conviction occurred before any investigation.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Arrest and conviction are presented as identical stages.">Arrest and conviction are presented as identical stages.</button></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <h2>Read a complete community-safety file before recommending a response</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Fictional Northside Community Hub case file</h3>
    <p><b>Facility observations:</b> At 6:45 Monday morning, coordinator Lena Ortiz found the rear storage-door frame damaged. The inventory listed 24 loaner laptops on Sunday evening; 21 remained on Monday. No employee reported an injury or threat.</p>
    <p><b>Records:</b> A camera shows a person entering the storage hallway at 2:18 a.m. The person’s face is not visible, and the camera does not show the storage door or the laptops. The alarm log records the rear-door sensor opening at 2:21. The closing checklist says the door was locked at 9:05 Sunday evening.</p>
    <p><b>Witness account:</b> A neighbor reported hearing a metallic sound at about 2:20 but did not see a person or vehicle. The approximate time is consistent with the two electronic records, but the account supplies no identity.</p>
    <p><b>Official status:</b> Police recorded a report of suspected burglary and theft. The investigation remains open. No one has been arrested or charged, and police have not released the name of a suspect.</p>
    <p><b>Public correction:</b> The neighborhood newsletter replaced its headline <span class="ex">Laptop thief caught</span> with <span class="ex">Police investigate missing hub laptops</span>. Its correction states that the first headline was unsupported.</p>
    <p><b>Response pilot:</b> The hub repaired the door frame, added a second inventory check, improved rear lighting, and arranged a private way for staff and visitors to report security concerns. For six months, the hub will record use, access barriers, costs, reported incidents, and any unintended effects. A six-month change at one site will not by itself prove that one measure caused the result.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You recovered the missing property, camera limit, witness role, current legal stage, and evaluation boundary from the Northside file.">
    <h3>Evidence check: what can the file defend?</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Three loaner laptops were missing when Monday’s inventory was compared with Sunday’s list." data-hint="Compare the stated inventory totals, 24 and 21, across the two named times." data-fix="Three loaner laptops were missing when Monday’s inventory was compared with Sunday’s list."><p class="quiz-question">1. What property loss does the facility record directly establish?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Three loaner laptops were missing when Monday’s inventory was compared with Sunday’s list.">Three loaner laptops were missing when Monday’s inventory was compared with Sunday’s list.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Every device in the building was taken during an armed robbery.">Every device in the building was taken during an armed robbery.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The inventory proves who removed the laptops.">The inventory proves who removed the laptops.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="It shows a hallway entry at 2:18 but does not show a face, the storage door, or the laptops." data-hint="Preserve the visible action and all three listed camera limits." data-fix="The camera shows a hallway entry at 2:18 but not a face, the storage door, or the laptops."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which summary reports the camera evidence completely?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It shows a hallway entry at 2:18 but does not show a face, the storage door, or the laptops.">It shows a hallway entry at 2:18 but does not show a face, the storage door, or the laptops.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It clearly identifies the person and records the laptops being removed.">It clearly identifies the person and records the laptops being removed.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It contains no time or visible movement.">It contains no time or visible movement.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The account supports an approximate sound time consistent with the records, but it supplies no identity." data-hint="Use what the witness heard and preserve what the witness did not see." data-fix="The account supports an approximate sound time consistent with the records, but it supplies no identity."><p class="quiz-question">3. What does the neighbor’s account add?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The account supports an approximate sound time consistent with the records, but it supplies no identity.">The account supports an approximate sound time consistent with the records, but it supplies no identity.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The neighbor identified and convicted the person who entered.">The neighbor identified and convicted the person who entered.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The account proves the alarm and camera times are false.">The account proves the alarm and camera times are false.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Police are investigating suspected burglary and theft; no arrest or charge is reported." data-hint="Stop at the exact official stage and include the two explicitly absent later stages." data-fix="Police are investigating suspected burglary and theft; no arrest or charge is reported."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which sentence preserves the current official status?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Police are investigating suspected burglary and theft; no arrest or charge is reported.">Police are investigating suspected burglary and theft; no arrest or charge is reported.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A named defendant was convicted and sentenced on Monday.">A named defendant was convicted and sentenced on Monday.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The newsletter’s first headline created a legal conviction.">The newsletter’s first headline created a legal conviction.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The pilot can provide local evidence, but one short site result cannot by itself prove which measure caused a change." data-hint="Keep the value of the local pilot and its site, duration, and causal limits." data-fix="The pilot can provide local evidence, but one short site result cannot by itself prove which measure caused a change."><p class="quiz-question">5. What conclusion could the six-month response pilot support?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The pilot can provide local evidence, but one short site result cannot by itself prove which measure caused a change.">The pilot can provide local evidence, but one short site result cannot by itself prove which measure caused a change.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Any decline will prove that brighter lighting alone ended all crime everywhere.">Any decline will prove that brighter lighting alone ended all crime everywhere.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Because the pilot is limited, none of its records can ever be useful.">Because the pilot is limited, none of its records can ever be useful.</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the neutral update and evidence boundary</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="police are investigating a suspected burglary at the community hub" data-hint="Begin with Police are investigating, then add a suspected burglary and the location." data-fix="Police are investigating a suspected burglary at the community hub." data-success-message="Correct. The sentence names the investigation and suspected offense without inventing an arrest, identity, or conviction.">
    <h3>Build 1: report the official stage</h3><p class="tile-target">Use the current Northside police update.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="hub">hub</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="suspected">suspected</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="investigating">investigating</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="community">community</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="Police">Police</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="burglary">burglary</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="are">are</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="at">at</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="the video shows an entry but does not identify the person" data-hint="Begin with The video shows an entry, then add but does not identify the person." data-fix="The video shows an entry but does not identify the person." data-success-message="Correct. The first clause reports the visible event, and the second preserves the camera’s identity limit.">
    <h3>Build 2: state what the evidence cannot establish</h3><p class="tile-target">Keep the recorded entry and missing identity together.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="identify">identify</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="entry">entry</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="video">video</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="person">person</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="not">not</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="shows">shows</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="an">an</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="does">does</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="but">but</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair the inaccurate relationship</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="evidences" data-hint="Evidence is uncountable; count pieces when the number matters." data-fix="Investigators collected three relevant pieces of evidence." data-why="Evidence is uncountable in standard U.S. English, so three requires a countable unit such as pieces." data-success-message="Correct. The repair counts pieces instead of adding a plural ending to evidence.">
    <h3>Repair 1: count the evidence accurately</h3><p>Tap the word that incorrectly treats <span class="ex">evidence</span> as a count noun.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="investigators">Investigators collected</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="three">three relevant</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="evidences">evidences</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="case">for the case.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="robbed" data-hint="The sentence describes unauthorized entry into an apartment, not a person or institution targeted with force or threat." data-fix="Someone broke into the apartment while the residents were away." data-why="Break into describes unauthorized entry to a building in everyday speech; rob normally takes the affected person or institution." data-success-message="Correct. The repair now names unauthorized entry without forcing the apartment into the object pattern of rob.">
    <h3>Repair 2: choose the participant required by the verb</h3><p>Tap the verb that does not fit the supplied unauthorized-entry context.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="someone">Someone</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="robbed">robbed</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="apartment">the apartment</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="away">while the residents were away.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="criminal" data-hint="The record reports questioning during an open investigation and no charge." data-fix="Police questioned a suspect, but no one has been charged." data-why="Questioning and suspicion do not establish guilt; suspect preserves the open legal stage stated in the record." data-success-message="Correct. Suspect now reports possible involvement without converting the investigation into a conviction.">
    <h3>Repair 3: preserve the presumption boundary</h3><p>Tap the noun that declares guilt before the stated process has established it.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="police">Police questioned</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="criminal">the criminal,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="but">but no one</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="charged">has been charged.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Practice a neutral briefing without disclosing a real experience</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to reveal a real victimization, accusation, arrest, court case, immigration matter, home address, financial loss, identity document, workplace incident, family conflict, police contact, security routine, political belief, or traumatic event. Use Northside, a tutor-supplied fictional case, or a public record the learner freely chooses. Do not ask a learner to perform a criminal role from personal experience.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Incident map:</b> Name the reported act, affected property or person, time and place, source, direct evidence, missing information, and current legal stage.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Headline repair:</b> Replace guilt language with a source, an allegation or investigation frame, the strongest supported fact, and one important limit.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Process check:</b> Put investigate, arrest, charge, trial, convict or acquit, and sentence in the order supported by the record. Omit stages the record does not contain.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Response check:</b> Propose support and prevention, then name the target, cost or trade-off, fairness concern, timeframe, and evidence that would justify continuing.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: deliver a 90-second fictional community-safety briefing</h3>
    <p>Use the Northside file. Name the reported offenses and affected property; distinguish facility observations, electronic records, and the witness account; state what the video shows and cannot show; correct the unsupported headline; report the current investigation stage; use one accurate steal or break-into pattern; explain the hub’s support and prevention pilot; identify one fairness or access concern; recommend one six-month measure; and answer one skeptical community question. Use at least six target chunks and make <span class="ex">theft, burglary, evidence</span>, the noun <span class="ex">SUSpect</span>, and the verb <span class="ex">susPECT</span> intelligible.</p>
    <p><b>Evidence check:</b> Can the listener reconstruct the act, affected property, sources, observable evidence, missing identity, allegation status, current legal stage, response purpose, evaluation limit, and responsible next step without hearing an unsupported claim of guilt?</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You preserved offense meanings, verb patterns, uncountable evidence, legal stages, reported-data limits, and a measurable community response.">
    <h3>Final check: choose the report the evidence can defend</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Someone stole a laptop from the office after breaking into the locked storage room." data-hint="Use steal for the thing taken and break into for unauthorized entry to the room." data-fix="Someone stole a laptop from the office after breaking into the locked storage room."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which sentence keeps the missing property and unauthorized entry in their natural verb patterns?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Someone stole a laptop from the office after breaking into the locked storage room.">Someone stole a laptop from the office after breaking into the locked storage room.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Someone robbed a laptop of the office after stealing into the room.">Someone robbed a laptop of the office after stealing into the room.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A laptop broke the office into someone.">A laptop broke the office into someone.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The file contains several pieces of evidence, but none of them identifies the person in the video." data-hint="Count pieces of evidence and preserve the file’s identity limit." data-fix="The file contains several pieces of evidence, but none identifies the person in the video."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence uses <span class="ex">evidence</span> accurately and reports its limit?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The file contains several pieces of evidence, but none of them identifies the person in the video.">The file contains several pieces of evidence, but none of them identifies the person in the video.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The file contains several evidences that automatically convict the person.">The file contains several evidences that automatically convict the person.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="One evidence means no investigation can exist.">One evidence means no investigation can exist.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="A suspect was arrested and charged, but the case has not reached a verdict." data-hint="Keep arrest and charge separate from the later trial outcome." data-fix="A suspect was arrested and charged, but the case has not reached a verdict."><p class="quiz-question">3. In a different fictional case, police made an arrest and prosecutors filed a charge, but no trial has ended. Which update is accurate?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A suspect was arrested and charged, but the case has not reached a verdict.">A suspect was arrested and charged, but the case has not reached a verdict.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The arrested person was automatically convicted and sentenced before trial.">The arrested person was automatically convicted and sentenced before trial.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A charge means the defendant was acquitted.">A charge means the defendant was acquitted.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The video shows an entry at 2:18, but it does not identify the person or show the laptops being removed." data-hint="Retain both the recorded entry and the two relevant gaps." data-fix="The video shows an entry at 2:18, but it does not identify the person or show the laptops being removed."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which sentence calibrates the Northside camera evidence correctly?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The video shows an entry at 2:18, but it does not identify the person or show the laptops being removed.">The video shows an entry at 2:18, but it does not identify the person or show the laptops being removed.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The video proves the identity and records every act inside the storage room.">The video proves the identity and records every act inside the storage room.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Because the face is unclear, the timestamp and entry cannot exist.">Because the face is unclear, the timestamp and entry cannot exist.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The increase may reflect easier reporting, a change in incidents, or both; the agency needs comparable data." data-hint="A reporting form and recorded count changed together, so preserve more than one explanation." data-fix="The increase may reflect easier reporting, a change in incidents, or both; comparable data is needed."><p class="quiz-question">5. Recorded reports rose just after an easier reporting form launched. Which interpretation is defensible?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The increase may reflect easier reporting, a change in incidents, or both; the agency needs comparable data.">The increase may reflect easier reporting, a change in incidents, or both; the agency needs comparable data.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The form proves every additional report represents a new offense caused by the form.">The form proves every additional report represents a new offense caused by the form.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Recorded reports always equal every incident that occurred.">Recorded reports always equal every incident that occurred.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Pilot secure storage for six months, track use, access, costs, and comparable reports, then review whether to continue." data-hint="Choose the proposal with a target action, timeframe, relevant measures, access check, cost, and later decision." data-fix="Pilot secure storage for six months, track use, access, costs, and comparable reports, then review whether to continue."><p class="quiz-question">6. Which community response produces useful evidence without promising to end every offense?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Pilot secure storage for six months, track use, access, costs, and comparable reports, then review whether to continue.">Pilot secure storage for six months, track use, access, costs, and comparable reports, then review whether to continue.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Install one sign and announce that all crime has permanently ended.">Install one sign and announce that all crime has permanently ended.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Ask affected people to accept responsibility for every future incident.">Ask affected people to accept responsibility for every future incident.</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect: what has the record established at each stage?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the reporting path</h3>
    <p>Complete these ideas aloud: <span class="ex">Theft differs from robbery because...</span> <span class="ex">Steal differs from rob because...</span> <span class="ex">A suspect is not a convicted person because...</span> <span class="ex">Charged with differs from convicted of because...</span> <span class="ex">Evidence is uncountable, so...</span> <span class="ex">Unverified does not mean...</span> <span class="ex">Reported crime does not automatically equal...</span> <span class="ex">A fair prevention pilot should measure...</span></p>
    <p>Take one sensational fictional headline and rebuild it as a four-sentence update. Name the source, strongest supported observation, evidence limit, current legal stage, and responsible next action. Then explain which original word created unsupported certainty.</p>
    <p><a href="#next-day-retrieval">Return tomorrow for the five-item retrieval check</a> before rereading the lesson.</p>
  </div>

  <section id="next-day-retrieval" data-lesson-extension="Next-day offense distinction, steal-rob pattern, legal-stage relationship, evidence boundary, and reported-crime response retrieval">
    <h2>Next-day retrieval</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <p>Return without rereading the page. Recover the offense meaning, verb participant, legal stage, evidence limit, and evaluable community response.</p>
    <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You retained the robbery distinction, steal-rob participant pattern, charge-conviction boundary, evidence limit, and structure of a measurable response.">
      <h3>Five delayed checks</h3>
      <div class="quiz-list">
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Robbery includes force or threat in the supplied act; basic theft does not require that element." data-hint="Use the threat as the decisive detail in the lesson’s everyday distinction." data-fix="Robbery includes force or threat in the supplied act; basic theft does not require that element."><p class="quiz-question">1. A person threatens a cashier and takes money. Why does the lesson classify the act as robbery rather than basic theft?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Robbery includes force or threat in the supplied act; basic theft does not require that element.">Robbery includes force or threat in the supplied act; basic theft does not require that element.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Robbery means any missing object with no person or threat.">Robbery means any missing object with no person or threat.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The two words always have identical legal definitions everywhere.">The two words always have identical legal definitions everywhere.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Someone stole a phone from the passenger; the passenger was robbed." data-hint="Steal takes the thing; rob takes the affected person." data-fix="Someone stole a phone from the passenger; the passenger was robbed."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence tracks the property and affected person naturally?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Someone stole a phone from the passenger; the passenger was robbed.">Someone stole a phone from the passenger; the passenger was robbed.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Someone robbed a phone from the passenger; the phone was stolen a person.">Someone robbed a phone from the passenger; the phone was stolen a person.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The passenger stole into the phone.">The passenger stole into the phone.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The charge is a formal accusation; conviction requires a later guilty outcome in the legal process." data-hint="Separate filing the offense from establishing guilt at a later stage." data-fix="A charge is a formal accusation; a conviction is a later guilty outcome."><p class="quiz-question">3. Why does <span class="ex">charged with fraud</span> not mean <span class="ex">convicted of fraud</span>?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The charge is a formal accusation; conviction requires a later guilty outcome in the legal process.">The charge is a formal accusation; conviction requires a later guilty outcome in the legal process.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A charge is the penalty imposed after every appeal.">A charge is the penalty imposed after every appeal.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Convicted of means police have only started asking questions.">Convicted of means police have only started asking questions.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The video establishes an entry time, but it does not establish the person’s identity or the removal of property." data-hint="Recover one visible fact and the two gaps from the Northside camera." data-fix="The video establishes an entry time, but not identity or removal of property."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which sentence preserves the Northside video’s evidence boundary?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The video establishes an entry time, but it does not establish the person’s identity or the removal of property.">The video establishes an entry time, but it does not establish the person’s identity or the removal of property.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The entry time automatically identifies and convicts a person.">The entry time automatically identifies and convicts a person.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="An unclear face erases every other visible detail.">An unclear face erases every other visible detail.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Test the measure for a defined period, compare relevant records, use, access, and costs, then make the next decision." data-hint="Choose the sequence that links a limited action to evidence and a review point." data-fix="Test the measure for a defined period, compare relevant records, use, access, and costs, then make the next decision."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which structure makes a community-safety proposal evaluable?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Test the measure for a defined period, compare relevant records, use, access, and costs, then make the next decision.">Test the measure for a defined period, compare relevant records, use, access, and costs, then make the next decision.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Promise that one measure will end every offense and collect no data.">Promise that one measure will end every offense and collect no data.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Ignore affected people, access, cost, and unintended effects.">Ignore affected people, access, cost, and unintended effects.</button></div></div>
      </div>
